`(x) => ...` writes memory its caller can see at tests/wordings/nl2345_par_shared_write_map_arrow.ts:13:5, and `parallelMap` runs it on several threads at once: a parallel body may read what its caller owns and write nothing but its result; make it answer what it computes and do the write after the call, or run it on the thread that called it, `const doubled: i32[] = []; for (const x of src) { seen.n = x; doubled.push(x * 2) }`
